<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{DOMAIN}} · getBible API</title>
{{HEAD_ICONS}}<style>{{CSS}}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<header class="brand">
{{#IF LOGO_URL}}<a href="/"><img src="{{LOGO_URL}}" alt="getBible"></a>
{{/IF}}<div>
<h1>{{DOMAIN}}</h1>
<p class="lead">The getBible <strong>{{KIND}}</strong> API: {{DESCRIPTION}}. <span class="badge">{{ACCESS_MODE_LABEL}}</span></p>
</div>
</header>

<h2>Endpoints</h2>
<p>Every path starts with a version segment. Each version is served by its own service and has its own documentation page and OpenAPI document.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Version</th><th>Route</th><th>Documentation</th><th>OpenAPI</th></tr>
{{ENDPOINT_ROWS}}
</table>

<h2>How to call it</h2>
<pre><code>curl https://{{DOMAIN}}/{{EXAMPLE_PATH}}</code></pre>
<ul>
<li>Responses are JSON with open CORS (<code>Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *</code>); preflights answer <code>204</code>.</li>
<li>Health: <code>GET /healthz</code>; readiness (the service can read scripture): <code>GET /readyz</code>.</li>
<li>Every error is an <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457">RFC 9457 problem document</a> (<code>application/problem+json</code>).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Access</h2>
{{ACCESS_HTML}}

<footer>{{#IF ICON_URL}}<img src="{{ICON_URL}}" alt="">{{/IF}}Served by getBible · <a href="https://getbible.net">getbible.net</a> · Requests carry an <code>X-Request-ID</code> header; quote it when reporting a problem.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
